
<p>Re: my post today <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/10/real_artists_ship_tesla_edition">on the still-vaporware Tesla Roadster</a> and Benedict Evans’s maxim that “Elon Musk is a bullshitter who delivers”, a reader sent me <a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/p5vm2n49qp8">this YouTube short</a> of Charlie Munger’s answer to a question at Berkshire Hathaway’s 2020 shareholder meeting regarding Tesla’s volatility and Musk’s self-promotion. Munger said:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>My thoughts are two. I would never buy it, and I would never sell
it short.</p>

<p>[<em>Audience laughs.</em>]</p>

<p>I have a third comment. There was a man out in Los Angeles for
years named Howard Ahmanson. He once said something that I’ve taken
to my heart: “Never underestimate the man who overestimates
himself.” I think Elon Musk is peculiar and he may overestimate
himself, but he may not be wrong all the time.</p>
</blockquote>

